{"name":"Dairy Made","hex":"#f0b33c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dairy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(also dairy products or dairy produce) Products produced from milk.","A place that produces, processes, or sells such products:\nA place, often on a farm, where milk is processed and turned into products such as butter and cheese."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Referring to products produced from milk.\n Referring to products produced from animal milk as opposed to non-milk substitutes.","Referring to products produced from animal milk as opposed to non-milk substitutes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dairy"},{"term":"made","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A grub or maggot."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of make","simple past and past participle of myek"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/made"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dairy","blocks":[{"text":"A dairy farm is a place where milk is stored and where butter, cheese, and other dairy products are made, or a place where those products are sold. It may be a room, a building, or a larger establishment. In the United States, the word may also describe a dairy farm or the part of a mixed farm dedicated to milk for human consumption, whether from cows, buffaloes, goats, yaks, sheep, horses or camels."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Alte_Batzenalpe_2014_Interior_06.jpg/330px-Alte_Batzenalpe_2014_Interior_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dairy","wikidata":"Q637776"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Sumerian_scene%2C_milking_cows_and_making_dairy_products._From_the_facade_of_the_Temple_of_Ninhursag_at_Tell_al-%27Ubaid%2C_Iraq%2C_2800-2600_BCE._Iraq_Museum.jpg/500px-Sumerian_scene%2C_milking_cows_and_making_dairy_products._From_the_facade_of_the_Temple_of_Ninhursag_at_Tell_al-%27Ubaid%2C_Iraq%2C_2800-2600_BCE._Iraq_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Sumerian_scene%2C_milking_cows_and_making_dairy_products._From_the_facade_of_the_Temple_of_Ninhursag_at_Tell_al-%27Ubaid%2C_Iraq%2C_2800-2600_BCE._Iraq_Museum.jpg/1280px-Sumerian_scene%2C_milking_cows_and_making_dairy_products._From_the_facade_of_the_Temple_of_Ninhursag_at_Tell_al-%27Ubaid%2C_Iraq%2C_2800-2600_BCE._Iraq_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Sumerian_scene%2C_milking_cows_and_making_dairy_products._From_the_facade_of_the_Temple_of_Ninhursag_at_Tell_al-%27Ubaid%2C_Iraq%2C_2800-2600_BCE._Iraq_Museum.jpg/500px-Sumerian_scene%2C_milking_cows_and_making_dairy_products._From_the_facade_of_the_Temple_of_Ninhursag_at_Tell_al-%27Ubaid%2C_Iraq%2C_2800-2600_BCE._Iraq_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Frieze of the Dairy\" showing the façade of the temple of the goddess Ninhursag at Tell al-Ubaid, 2800-2600 BCE, depicting the production of cow dairy products in the stables of the complex, with aman milking on the right and, on the left, men decanting and churning in large containers to obtain cream, butter and cheese, Sumerian Gallery of the Iraq Museum[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASumerian_scene%2C_milking_cows_and_making_dairy_products._From_the_facade_of_the_Temple_of_Ninhursag_at_Tell_al-'Ubaid%2C_Iraq%2C_2800-2600_BCE._Iraq_Museum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/The_Women%27s_Land_Army_in_Britain%2C_1915-1918_Q30682.jpg/500px-The_Women%27s_Land_Army_in_Britain%2C_1915-1918_Q30682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/